ex, the hyperedge {v}. (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"loop a zero column; Godsil–Royle’s entry 2 is not a bit. A zero column would forget the loop.)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the directed form; ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation of the same hypergraphs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Both orientations are stored, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" stores its rows: n rows of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the row and column popcounts cached. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are each one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swaps the two in O(1). The cost is 2·n·m\/8 bytes: "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the matrix is for dense or small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (spectral work at n·m up to about 10⁹, hypergraphs with large hyperedges). Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence belongs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape: column order is observable, because a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column’s position is what a spectral caller indexes by. ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"’s equality"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignores positions; convert to compare that way.)"}]}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"title":"IncidenceMatrix","remoteSource":{"fileName":"IncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix.swift#L28"},"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V"},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/init(vertexCount:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"init(vertexCount:)","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/init(vertexcount:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A matrix of "},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" vertices and no columns."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vertexCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(vertexCount:)"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/Encodable-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmod